## 📍 HoudahGeo Geotagging for Mac

**HoudahGeo for Mac** is a dedicated photo and video geocoding and geotagging application from Houdah Software. It helps photographers connect media with precise geographic information using GPS track logs, reference photos, interactive maps, waypoints and manual coordinates. HoudahGeo can then write location information into supported metadata formats such as EXIF, XMP and IPTC.

<div align="left">

> 📍 **Precise Locations:** Add latitude, longitude and altitude information to photos and videos.
> 🛰️ **GPS Track Logs:** Match media timestamps with recorded GPS routes.
> 🗺️ **Interactive Maps:** Review and manually adjust locations using the map interface.
> 📷 **Reference Photos:** Use GPS-enabled smartphone photos to help position other images.
> 🧩 **Metadata:** Add location names, descriptions, titles and keywords.
> 🎥 **Video Support:** HoudahGeo 7 adds geotagging support for video files.
> 🍎 **Apple Silicon:** HoudahGeo 7 runs natively on Apple Silicon Macs.

## 🛰️ GPS Tracklog Geotagging

HoudahGeo can automatically match photos and videos to GPS track logs by comparing their timestamps with recorded routes. This is useful when a camera does not have built-in GPS but you carry a phone or dedicated GPS logger while traveling.

<div align="left">

> 🛰️ **GPX Support:** Import GPS Exchange Format track logs into your project.
> ⏱️ **Timestamp Matching:** Match media to GPS positions based on capture times.
> 🧭 **Route Interpolation:** Determine positions between recorded track points.
> 📌 **Waypoints:** Assign media to manually recorded GPS waypoints.
> 🗺️ **Route Review:** Inspect matched locations on the built-in map.
> ⚙️ **Camera Clock:** Adjust camera time information when timestamps do not match the GPS track.
> 🔄 **Reprocessing:** Rerun geocoding when settings or source information changes.

</div>

## 🗺️ Interactive Map & Manual Geocoding

Not every photo needs a GPS track. HoudahGeo provides manual location tools for images where GPS data is missing or inaccurate.

<div align="left">

> 🗺️ **Map Placement:** Choose a location manually on the map.
> 📍 **Drag & Drop:** Position photos at selected map locations.
> 🔎 **Location Search:** Search for places through the map interface.
> 🛰️ **Satellite View:** Switch map presentation when additional visual context is useful.
> 📌 **Saved Places:** Use known locations and favorite places in your workflow.
> 🎯 **Coordinate Entry:** Enter latitude and longitude when exact coordinates are already known.
> 🔧 **Location Correction:** Review and refine automatically assigned locations.

## 📷 Reference Photo Geocoding

HoudahGeo can use photos from a GPS-enabled smartphone or another GPS-equipped camera as location references. This makes it possible to transfer location information to images captured by cameras without GPS.

<div align="left">

> 📱 **Smartphone Reference:** Use a GPS-tagged phone photo as a location reference.
> 📷 **Camera Pairing:** Match reference images with photos from another camera.
> ⏱️ **Time-Based Matching:** Propagate location information according to photo timestamps.
> 🎯 **Time Gap Control:** Define how far apart images can be while sharing a location.
> 🌍 **Mixed Camera Workflow:** Combine smartphone and dedicated-camera images in one project.
> ⚙️ **Clock Correction:** Account for differences between camera and reference-photo timestamps.

</div>

## 🧩 EXIF, XMP & IPTC Metadata

Geotagging becomes particularly useful when location information is written into media metadata rather than kept only inside a particular photo library.

<div align="left">

> 🧩 **EXIF:** Store geographic and camera-related information using standard image metadata.
> 📝 **XMP:** Work with XMP metadata and sidecar files where appropriate.
> 🏷️ **IPTC:** Add descriptive metadata alongside geographic information.
> 📍 **Coordinates:** Store latitude and longitude with the media.
> ⛰️ **Altitude:** Preserve elevation information when available.
> 🧭 **Heading:** Keep supported direction information from GPS data.
> 🔑 **Keywords:** Add searchable location and descriptive keywords.
> 🏙️ **Place Names:** Enrich coordinates with country, province and city information.

</div>

