## 🔐 Metadata & Backup Notes

Because geotagging can write information directly into media files, a careful backup workflow is recommended before exporting metadata.

<div align="left">

> 🛡️ **Backup First:** Keep backup copies before modifying original files.
> 🧩 **Lossless Metadata:** HoudahGeo's documented metadata-writing process does not alter image quality.
> 📁 **Sidecars:** XMP sidecars can be used for supported workflows.
> 💾 **Temporary Space:** Metadata export may require temporary disk space.
> ⚠️ **Memory Cards:** Avoid writing metadata directly to memory cards when possible.
> 📷 **Original Protection:** Use copies during export when an additional safety layer is desired.

</div>

## ❓ HoudahGeo for Mac – FAQ

<div align="left">

### ❔ What is HoudahGeo?

📍 HoudahGeo is a Mac application for photo and video geocoding and geotagging.

### ❔ Can HoudahGeo geotag videos?

🎥 Yes. HoudahGeo 7 introduced video geotagging support.

### ❔ Can I use a GPX track with HoudahGeo?

🛰️ Yes. GPS track logs can be imported and matched against media timestamps.

### ❔ Can I manually place photos on a map?

🗺️ Yes. HoudahGeo allows manual location placement and correction through its map workflow.

### ❔ Does HoudahGeo work with Apple Photos?

🍎 Yes. HoudahGeo can work with Apple Photos and can update location and metadata information.

### ❔ Does HoudahGeo support Lightroom?

🖼️ Yes. The current HoudahGeo 7 media browser supports working with Adobe Lightroom libraries.

### ❔ Which metadata formats are supported?

🧩 HoudahGeo works with EXIF, XMP and IPTC metadata for supported media workflows.

### ❔ What macOS version does HoudahGeo 7 require?

💻 HoudahGeo 7 requires macOS 12.4 or later.

### ❔ Can HoudahGeo export maps?

🌎 Yes. It supports Google Earth KML/KMZ workflows as well as customizable CSV exports.

